From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 16:02:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] configstore: add TableTenant and customer.tenant_id
 (Phase 1 schema starter)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

First migration of the multi-tenant Phase 1 rollout. Creates a
bf_tenants table at the platform level (above governance), seeds a
"default" tenant so existing single-tenant deployments keep working,
adds tenant_id to governance_customers with a "default" default, and
backfills any pre-existing customer rows to the default tenant.

This is the pattern for the rest of the governance tables (teams,
virtual_keys, budgets, rate_limits, provider_configs) — keeping each
table's tenant_id rollout as its own migration commit makes review
tractable.

Backward-compatible by construction: single-tenant deployments observe
no behavior change (every customer belongs to tenant=default).

Tests:
  - TestTriggerMigrations_FreshDB now asserts bf_tenants exists
  - TestMigrationAddTenants_CreatesTableAndSeedsDefault asserts the
    default tenant is seeded, the column default kicks in for new
    customer inserts, and the migration is idempotent on re-run

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
